    description: "WHY. The statement records cannot speak for 8,107 tests the index calls unmeasured. 5,403 of them have a static path to package source; 2,629 have none. 3,109 of the unmeasured are the tracker package's (its own item decides whether to measure it).\n\nWHAT. In the by-statement selector: an unmeasured test with a static path to package source is selected by walking the stored graph from the changed files; one with no path stays under today's rules (the top-level map, the read records, the declared gates).\n\nCLOSE CONDITION. The same shadow bar as the selector's, counted SEPARATELY for this group: runs with a failed unmeasured test, and how many fell outside the selection. Re-state the three counts above from the current index; they were measured on 2026-11-15.\n\nSOURCE. ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_plan_11152026.md; the owner's rulings of 2026-11-17 are its second 'Made' table. Measurements: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_followup_11172026/README.md, slice_graph_11152026/README.md, stale_graph_1a_11152026/README.md, fast_smart_test_11152026/README.md (the 37-PR replay)."  # 3125
